Not applied anywhere: what the V8-side fix would look like, for reference.
fibers requires --no-turbo-fast-api-calls instead (see checkFlags in fibers.js).

Since V8 12.4 (dd8d0b44d5, "[execution] Support stack iteration from fast C
calls"), StackFrameIterator::Reset(ThreadLocalTop*) starts from the isolate-wide
fast_c_call_caller_fp whenever it is set, whichever thread it was asked to walk.
During a GC that starts inside a fast C call, every archived thread (every
suspended fiber) is then walked from the running thread's frame and its own
stack is skipped. Against Node 26.13.1 (V8 14.6.202.34). Untested: never built.

